# Workflow plan step C2 (docs/WORKFLOW_PLAN.md, 2026-11-14): CalculiX results in the app. The beam starter run in ccx: Results
# gives the largest displacement and von Mises stress, the safety factor against steel's yield, and beside it the
# Euler-Bernoulli hand calculation (0.1905 mm against FE); the reactions aren't written, so the button adds RF to the output,
# and after another run they balance the 1 kN load. A side view of the deformed beam, coloured by stress.
action go.new
wait-until page New case
click new-prog:calculix
wait 5
click label:Cantilever beam
wait 5
click clone-name
key A ctrl
type c2beam
click clone-go
wait-until page Overview timeout 10
click nav:run
wait-until page Run
click run-go
wait-until job finished timeout 120
wait 20
click nav:results
wait-until page Results
wait 30
assert text The answer
assert text Largest displacement 0.19
assert text Largest von Mises stress
assert text Safety factor
assert text Hand calculation: tip deflection 0.1905 mm
assert text Reactions not written
click ccx-working
wait 5
assert text I = b h^3 / 12
screenshot $OUT/c2_answer.png
click ccx-add-rf
wait 10
shell grep -q '^U, RF$' $SB/home/calculix/c2beam/beam.inp && touch $OUT/rf-ok
assert file $OUT/rf-ok
click nav:run
wait-until page Run
click run-go
wait-until job finished timeout 120
wait 20
click nav:results
wait-until page Results
wait 60
assert text Reactions at the supports
assert text They balance the loads
screenshot $OUT/c2_reactions.png
wheel -6
wait 10
screenshot $OUT/c2_view.png
